{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_e28e5cc34fcd4eb691f9c0d9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tWrite a Zephyr RTOS application that performs an SPI loopback test.\n2\t\n3\tRequirements:\n4\t1. Get the SPI bus device using DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(spi0))\n5\t2. Verify the device is initialized and ready before use\n6\t3. Define a transmit buffer of 8 bytes initialized with a known pattern (e.g., 0x01 through 0x08)\n7\t4. Define a receive buffer of 8 bytes initialized to zero\n8\t5. Configure struct spi_config with frequency 1000000, operation SPI_OP_MODE_MASTER | SPI_WORD_SET(8)\n9\t6. Set up struct spi_buf for tx and rx, each pointing to their respective buffers with len = 8\n10\t7. Set up struct spi_buf_set for tx_bufs and rx_bufs, each with buf pointer and count = 1\n11\t8. Call spi_transceive() with the spi_config, tx_bufs, and rx_bufs\n12\t9. Check the return value for errors; print error and return on failure\n13\t10. Compare transmit and receive buffers byte-by-byte to verify loopback\n14\t11. Print \"SPI loopback successful\" on match, \"SPI loopback mismatch\" on failure\n15\t\n16\tUse the Zephyr SPI API: spi_transceive, struct spi_config, struct spi_buf, struct spi_buf_set.\n17\t\n18\tInclude proper headers: zephyr/kernel.h, zephyr/device.h, zephyr/drivers/spi.h, string.h.\n19\t\n20\tOutput ONLY the complete C source file.\n21\t\n22\t\n23\tSubmission instruction: write the complete C source to submission/main.c using file tools instead of returning it in chat. Do not access paths outside this task workspace.\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2474aa5-6e9d-4cce-bc07-c1eddf4f2308","uuid":"b925c98a-4ec7-465c-8310-546d8bcfece8","timestamp":"2026-10-20T07:45:42.903Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"D:\\firmware-test\\experiments\\2026-10-20-qwen38-27b-harness-comparison\\runs\\run-20261020-154440-282906\\tasks\\claude-code__spi-i2c-002__1\\6bf52445\\workspace\\task.md","content":"Write a Zephyr RTOS application that performs an SPI loopback test.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Get the SPI bus device using DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(spi0))\n2. Verify the device is initialized and ready before use\n3. Define a transmit buffer of 8 bytes initialized with a known pattern (e.g., 0x01 through 0x08)\n4. Define a receive buffer of 8 bytes initialized to zero\n5. Configure struct spi_config with frequency 1000000, operation SPI_OP_MODE_MASTER | SPI_WORD_SET(8)\n6. Set up struct spi_buf for tx and rx, each pointing to their respective buffers with len = 8\n7. Set up struct spi_buf_set for tx_bufs and rx_bufs, each with buf pointer and count = 1\n8. Call spi_transceive() with the spi_config, tx_bufs, and rx_bufs\n9. Check the return value for errors; print error and return on failure\n10. Compare transmit and receive buffers byte-by-byte to verify loopback\n11. Print \"SPI loopback successful\" on match, \"SPI loopback mismatch\" on failure\n\nUse the Zephyr SPI API: spi_transceive, struct spi_config, struct spi_buf, struct spi_buf_set.\n\nInclude proper headers: zephyr/kernel.h, zephyr/device.h, zephyr/drivers/spi.h, string.h.\n\nOutput ONLY the complete C source file.\n\n\nSubmission instruction: write the complete C source to submission/main.c using file tools instead of returning it in chat. Do not access paths outside this task workspace.\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_e28e5cc34fcd4eb691f9c0d9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
